01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Lo and Behold, Reveries of the Connected World is a 2016
American documentary film directed by Werner Herzog.

11
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
In it, Herzog ponders the existential impact of such things as the Internet, robotics,
artificial intelligence, and the Internet of things on modern human life.

12
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The leaders in the field of technology who are interviewed in the film include
Leonard Kleinrock, Bob Kahn, Ted Nelson, Sebastian Thrun, and Elon Musk.

13
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:54,000
The film, which was sponsored by the company NetScout,
premiered at the 2016 Sundance Film Festival.

14
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:30,000
The film explores themes of artificial intelligence (a.i.),
planet mars, hacker, solar flare, space.
